# SILA Generate Hooks

## After Any File Modification

Automatically:

1. Detect impacted module
2. Validate imports
3. Validate architecture boundaries
4. Run targeted lint/type checks
5. Detect circular dependencies
6. Generate concise mutation summary

---

## After Python Changes

Run:

pytest -q --tb=short

If module-specific:

pytest apps/backend/app/modules/<MODULE>/tests -q

---

## After Router Changes

Validate:
- route registration
- OpenAPI integrity
- dependency injection consistency
- middleware compatibility

---

## After Repository Changes

Validate:
- BaseRepository contracts
- async session integrity
- transaction safety
- SQLAlchemy compatibility

---

## After Infrastructure Changes

Validate:
- Docker compatibility
- Redis connectivity
- Celery startup
- PostgreSQL connectivity

---

## After Consolidation Operations

Mandatory sequence:

make clean-audit
make daily-audit
cat reports/daily_audit.md

Generate:
- compliance summary
- circular dependency report
- module integrity report

---

## Architecture Enforcement

Never allow:
- circular imports
- infrastructure leaking into domain
- direct sibling module imports
- duplicated repositories
- duplicated services
- duplicated adapters

All cross-module communication must occur through:
- ports
- adapters
- X-Road interoperability

---

## Context Preservation Rule

Never recursively scan full repository.

Always:
1. search via docs/tree.md
2. locate via grep/find
3. read only relevant files

---

## Safe Refactor Rule

Before destructive operations:
- verify extraction success
- verify tests
- verify imports
- generate migration summary

Never purge before successful audit.

---

## Mutation Safety

For every mutation:
- explain root cause
- explain affected layers
- explain risk level
- explain rollback path